                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Change in Object Clause in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Object Clause (Clause III MOA) defines legal business scope. Change requires: Board Meeting, EGM Special Resolution (75%), MGT-14 with linked e-MOA (INC-33) and NIC Code within 30 days, ROC registration, fresh COI. No INC-24 needed (unlike name change). Activities outside objects are ultra vires (void). Delhi companies diversifying, pivoting, or seeking regulatory licences must amend. 10-20 working days. Patron manages from Delhi.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi NCR's dynamic business environment - startups pivoting, companies adding verticals, trading firms diversifying into tech, manufacturing adding exports - creates frequent need for object clause amendments. Ultra vires operations render contracts void. Learn more about <a href="/change-in-object-clause">Object Clause Change across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron Accounting's Delhi office handles complete object clause change: object drafting, NIC Code selection, resolution preparation, MGT-14 with e-MOA on MCA V3, ROC processing, fresh COI. Integrated with ROC compliance and <a href="/private-limited-company-registration">company registration</a>.</p>
