<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Object Clause: Clause III of the Memorandum of Association</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Clause III of MOA (S.4(1)(c)) states objects for which the company is incorporated. Under 2013 Act: (a) objects of the company, and (b) matters in furtherance. Differs from 1956 Act which had three categories.</p><p>Three functions: (1) defines and limits business scope, (2) informs shareholders, creditors, third parties, (3) binds directors to use funds only for stated objects. Activity outside objects = ultra vires = beyond legal powers. Contracts may be void.</p><p>Regular review essential as Delhi companies evolve, diversify, and expand. Patron reviews operations against MOA and identifies gaps requiring amendment.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Change in Object Clause in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Ultra Vires:</strong> Activities outside MOA objects. Beyond legal powers. Contracts potentially void. Director personal liability.</p><p><strong>NIC Code:</strong> National Industrial Classification 2008. Business activity classification in e-MOA. Must match new objects.</p><p><strong>MGT-14:</strong> Only form needed (no INC-24). Special Resolution + linked e-MOA (INC-33). Within 30 days.</p><p><strong>Fresh COI:</strong> Issued after ROC registers the alteration. Conclusive evidence of compliance.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
